title: FirstBudget_Start
tags:
---
<<wait_for_action grab_envelope>>
maya-didi: Khol le, na. Don't be shy. Count it.
<<wait_for_action count_cash>>
maya-didi: ₹15,000. That is everything you'll get this month.
maya-didi: First salary. Same as my first. Mine lasted nine days.
<<player_choose>>
-> Why only nine days?
    maya-didi: Because I had no plan. Money without a plan is rent
    maya-didi: for the next person's pocket. Today you make a plan.
    <<jump FirstBudget_ThreeEnvelopes>>
-> Just tell me what to do.
    maya-didi: Theek hai. No lecture. Three envelopes. Three buckets.
    <<jump FirstBudget_ThreeEnvelopes>>
===

title: FirstBudget_ThreeEnvelopes
tags:
---
<<wait_for_action open_drawer>>
maya-didi: See these three envelopes. Rent. Save. Spend.
maya-didi: Rent ka envelope sabse pehle. Always first.
maya-didi: Put ₹4,800 in Rent. That is what you owe Bhola Seth.
<<wait_for_action fill_envelope rent 4800>>
maya-didi: Good. Now Save. Put at least ₹2,000.
maya-didi: Not later. Now. Before you decide what to spend.
<<player_choose>>
-> Put ₹2,000 into Save.
    <<wait_for_action fill_envelope save 2000>>
    maya-didi: Achha. You paid yourself before you paid the world.
    <<set_flag paid_self_first>>
    <<jump FirstBudget_SpendRemainder>>
-> Put only ₹500 into Save.
    <<wait_for_action fill_envelope save 500>>
    maya-didi: Hmm. ₹500 is something. But ₹2,000 is a plan.
    maya-didi: Tell you what — try again. The envelope is paper, not stone.
    <<jump FirstBudget_RetrySave>>
-> Skip Save for now.
    maya-didi: Arre, no. That's the whole point of this drawer.
    maya-didi: Let's try once more. I'll wait.
    <<jump FirstBudget_RetrySave>>
===

title: FirstBudget_RetrySave
tags:
---
maya-didi: Look at it like this. ₹2,000 each month is ₹24,000 in a year.
maya-didi: That is one emergency you can swallow instead of borrow for.
<<wait_for_action fill_envelope save 2000>>
maya-didi: Better. Pay yourself first, every single time.
<<set_flag paid_self_first>>
<<jump FirstBudget_SpendRemainder>>
===

title: FirstBudget_SpendRemainder
tags:
---
maya-didi: Whatever is left — ₹8,200 — goes to Spend.
maya-didi: Chai, sabzi, bus pass, dabba. All of it from this envelope.
<<wait_for_action fill_envelope spend 8200>>
maya-didi: Now do the maths out loud. Income minus expenses equals…?
<<player_choose>>
-> Savings.
    maya-didi: Bilkul. Income minus expenses equals savings.
    maya-didi: That is the whole budget. The rest is decoration.
    <<set_flag understands_income_minus_expenses>>
-> Whatever is left.
    maya-didi: Close. We call "whatever is left" by a proper name —
    maya-didi: savings. Income minus expenses equals savings.
    <<set_flag understands_income_minus_expenses>>
<<continue>>
<<grant_mastery budgeting.income-expense 1>>
<<set_flag finished_first_budget>>
maya-didi: Tomorrow Aarav will try to sell you something stupid.
maya-didi: Now you have an envelope that can say no for you.
===
